  "live_records": {
    "q-124180": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124180",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(-1)-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
