    "q-124334": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124334",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14157978/assets/9c42d875a65a6b54ad7769180f5ec2e831772ad44a89ec913951da40c6d90514.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(-3,0)$ to the point $(0,2),$ as shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=2$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=2-0=2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
